p? Vote and explain your reasoning in the comments.","sponsored":false,"totalVotes":532,"startsAt":"2026-08-20T13:02:00Z","expiresAt":"2026-08-21T13:00:00Z","choices":[{"title":"Yes, buying","percent":49,"selected":false},{"title":"No, staying away","percent":27,"selected":false},{"title":"Just holding what I have","percent":7,"selected":false},{"title":"Watching from the sidelines","percent":17,"selected":false}],"winningChoice":1,"winningIndex":1,"associations":[{"type":"stock","id":"7745","symbol":"WMT","symbolDisplay":"WMT","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/WMT.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"12100","symbol":"BABA","symbolDisplay":"BABA","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/BABA.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"7396","symbol":"TGT","symbolDisplay":"TGT","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/TGT.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"7413","symbol":"TJX","symbolDisplay":"TJX","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/TJX.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"4996","symbol":"DKS","symbolDisplay":"DKS","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/DKS.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"9581","symbol":"QQQ","symbolDisplay":"QQQ","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/QQQ.png"}]},{"id":7192,"userId":9592203,"discussion":{"id":18665,"slug":"webull-bull-stock-is-rallying-on-a-q2-double-beat-are-you-buying-into-the-rally","indexed":true,"createdAt":"2026-08-20T13:01:27Z","discussionMessage":{"id":662395552,"body":"Webull ($BULL) stock is rallying on a Q2 double beat. Are you buying into the rally?","tokenizedBody":[{"type":"text","data":{"text":"Webull ("}},{"type":"cashTag","data":{"text":"$BULL","symbol":"BULL","symbolDisplay":"BULL","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/BULL.png","deeplink":"symbol/BULL"}},{"type":"text","data":{"text":") stock is rallying on a Q2 double beat. Are you buying into the rally?"}}],"createdAt":"2026-08-20T13:01:27Z","discussion":true,"discussionId":662395552,"discussionType":"poll","user":{"id":9592203,"username":"StocktwitsPolls","name":"Stocktwits Polls","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.stocktwits.com/production/9592203/thumb-1741199023.png","avatarUrlSsl":"https://avatars.stocktwits.com/production/9592203/thumb-1741199023.png","joinDate":"2024-11-18","official":true,"identity":"Official","classification":["suggested","official","premium","premium_edge"],"badges":[{"type":"official","showIcon":true}],"homeCountry":"US","searchRegions":[],"followers":68456,"following":3,"ideas":1474,"watchlistStocksCount":2,"likeCount":2,"plusTier":"","premiumRoom":"","tradeApp":false,"tradeStatus":"PENDING_MFA"},"source":{"id":1,"title":"Stocktwits","url":"https://stocktwits.com"},"symbols":[{"id":9655,"symbol":"BULL","symbolMic":"BULL.XNAS","symbolDisplay":"BULL","exchange":"NASDAQ","region":"US","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/BULL.png","title":"Webull Corp","aliases":[],"deeplink":"symbol/BULL","externalId":null,"isFollowing":false,"watchlistCount":24796,"hasPricing":true,"instrumentClass":"Stock","liveEvent":false,"sentimentChange":-1.86,"volumeChange":-2.38}],"conversation":{"parentMessageId":662395552,"inReplyToMessageId":null,"parent":true,"replies":1},"likes":{"total":6,"userIds":[6929661,3989296,8758166,459484,10021331,3819027]},"mentionedUsers":[],"entities":{"media":[],"sentiment":null}},"commentsCount":1},"status":"ended","question":"Webull ($BULL) stock is rallying on a Q2 double beat. Are you buying into the rally?","description":"Webull ($BULL) stock is surging after a Q2 double beat, with the rally compounding as broader crypto strength boosts trading activity across its platform. Are you buying into the $BULL rally? Vote and explain your reasoning in the comments.","sponsored":false,"totalVotes":709,"startsAt":"2026-08-20T12:59:00Z","expiresAt":"2026-08-21T12:00:00Z","choices":[{"title":"Yes, buying","percent":45,"selected":false},{"title":"No, not interested","percent":28,"selected":false},{"title":"Just holding what I have","percent":15,"selected":false},{"title":"Watching from the sidelines","percent":12,"selected":false}],"winningChoice":1,"winningIndex":1,"associations":[{"type":"stock","id":"9655","symbol":"BULL","symbolDisplay":"BULL","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/BULL.png"},{"type":"stock","id":"7271","symbol":"SPY","symbolDisplay":"SPY","logoUrl":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/SPY.png"}]}],"enableStaticSeoContent":true,"hasToken":false,"hideBottomAd":true,"homepageExperience":"authenticated-feed","referralCode":null,"newsArticles":[{"author":{"college_name":"","college_website_url":"","country":"India","description":"Anan Ashraf is a Staff Writer reporting on the US equities markets for Stocktwits, the largest social platform for investors and traders.\n\nHer primary coverage areas include the automotive sector, with a focus on electric vehicles, as well as the healthcare and biotechnology industries. In autos, she reports on production hurdles, delivery trends, new model rollouts, shifting EV demand, policy changes, and major capital investments. In the pharmaceutical and biotech industries, she tracks drug pipelines, clinical milestones, major licensing agreements, and mergers and acquisitions.\n\nBefore joining Stocktwits, Ashraf covered the “Future of Mobility” beat at Benzinga, concentrating on electric vehicles and the space industry. Earlier in her career, she contributed to Reuters, where she reported on company news across emerging Asian markets and Australian equities.","designation":"Staff Writer","education":"","email":"","id":21,"knows_about":"","name":"Anan Ashraf","profile_avatar":"https://news.stocktwits-cdn.com/unnamed_jpg_9dff551b50.webp","profile_link":"","skills":"","social_media_links":{"facebook":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/anan-ashraf/","twitter":"https://x.com/_AnanAshraf_","website":"https://stocktwits.com/Anan_Ashraf"},"type":"Stocktwits"},"canonical_url":"","category":{"id":2,"name":"Markets"},"content":"\u003cul class=\"summary-bullets\"\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Phase 3 HARBOR study compared the experimental drug with a dummy treatment in people with DM1, a progressive illness that stiffens and weakens muscles and has no approved medicine.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePatients did not open a clenched hand faster in a statistically meaningful way on the trial’s main measure.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe disappointment follows Friday’s failure of pelacarsen, Novartis’s late-stage heart drug licensed from Ionis Pharmaceuticals.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eNovartis shares (NVS) sold off hard on Tuesday after the company said a late-stage study of del-desiran in myotonic dystrophy type 1 failed its primary test, marking its second failed trial in a week.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe stock closed down 14%, clocking its worst day in over 20 years.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003eHand-Stiffness Test Falls Short\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Phase 3 HARBOR study compared the experimental drug with a dummy treatment in people with DM1, a progressive illness that stiffens and weakens muscles and has no approved medicine. Patients did not open a clenched hand faster in a statistically meaningful way on the trial’s main measure. Novartis said the drug showed signs of activity on secondary measures and that safety was in line with earlier studies. The company is reviewing the full data and will talk with regulators about next steps.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“Developing therapies for a complex disease like DM1 remains challenging, and setbacks are part of scientific progress,” said Shreeram Aradhye, Novartis’s president of development and chief medical officer.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDel-desiran came into the company through its $12 billion purchase of Avidity Biosciences. Novartis said work continues on two other drugs from that deal and that its longer-term sales growth outlook is unchanged.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003eA Second Miss In One Week\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe disappointment follows Friday’s failure of pelacarsen, Novartis’s late-stage heart drug licensed from Ionis Pharmaceuticals. That study lowered the targeted blood fat but did not cut the risk of heart attacks, strokes and related events.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“These are not the results we hoped for,” Aradhye said on Friday.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003eOther Stocks Slide; Analysts Split On Fallout\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eCompanies working on related muscle diseases moved with Novartis. Shares of Dyne Therapeutics (DYN), which is developing zbasivarsen for DM1, fell 16%. Sarepta Therapeutics (SRPT) was down 7%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eJefferies said the HARBOR miss “may negatively impact the space,” but argued Dyne’s zbasivarsen could still work and “even generate superior data.” The firm called Dyne the “frontrunner” in DM1 after Novartis’s failure and kept a Buy rating and $50 target.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStifel said many investors had treated HARBOR as likely to succeed and that Dyne will stay under pressure. The bear case, it said, is that the drugs look similar and Dyne’s pivotal study is smaller. Stifel still likes Dyne’s scientific case, would buy the selloff, and rates the stock Buy with a $37 target.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eH.C. Wainwright kept a Sell rating and $5 target on Sarepta. It said the miss is “particularly relevant” as support for Sarepta’s marketed Duchenne story has faded, and it raises the bar for Sarepta’s SRP-1003 being developed to treat DM1.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003eHow Did Retail Traders React?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eOn Stocktwits, retail sentiment around NVS stock remained ‘extremely bullish’ over the past 24 hours, while message volume rose from ‘high’ to ‘extremely high’ levels.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eA few Stocktwits users opined that Novartis should strengthen its pipeline with other buyouts.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstembedurl\u003ehttps://stocktwits.com/CityLife511/message/663805749\u003c/stembedurl\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstembedurl\u003ehttps://stocktwits.com/HalfTrader/message/663812506\u003c/stembedurl\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAnother user called Tuesday's selloff a good opportunity and expressed hopes for a recovery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstembedurl\u003ehttps://stocktwits.com/SenefAS/message/663779750\u003c/stembedurl\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://stocktwits.com/symbol/NVS\"\u003eNVS stock\u003c/a\u003e is trading flat year-to-date.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAlso See: \u003ca href=\"https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/nflx-is-opening-up-box-office-numbers-for-six-upcoming-films-says-report-is-netflix-rethinking-its-movie-theater-strategy/cZtE4kpRJyR\"\u003eNFLX Is Opening Up Box Office Numbers For Six Upcoming Films, Says Report — Is Netflix Rethinking Its Movie-Theater Strategy?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eFor updates and corrections, email newsroom[at]stocktwits[dot]com.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","created_at":"2026-09-08T20:09:14Z","featured_image":"https://st-everywhere-cms-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/large_novartis_stock_resized_978faa13aa.jpg","featured_image_attributes":{"alt_text":"In this photo illustration, the Novartis company logo is seen displayed on a smartphone screen. (Photo Illustration by Piotr Swat/SOPA Images/LightRocket via Getty Images)","caption":"In this photo illustration, the Novartis company logo is seen displayed on a smartphone screen. (Photo Illustration by Piotr Swat/SOPA Images/LightRocket via Getty Images)","url":"https://st-everywhere-cms-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/large_novartis_stock_resized_978faa13aa.jpg"},"headline":"NVS Stock Clocks Worst Day In Over 20 Years After Second Trial Failure In A Week — DYN, SRPT Slip In Sympathy","hero_article":true,"image_url":"https://st-everywhere-cms-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/large_novartis_stock_resized_978faa13aa.jpg","is_amp":true,"is_indexed":true,"meta_description":"The company said on Tuesday that its experimental drug del-desiran failed in a late-stage trial.","meta_keywords":"Novartis, NVS, myotonic dystrophy, Phase 3 HARBOR study, nvs stock, nvs shares, dyn stock, Dyn shares, srpt stock, srpt shares","meta_title":"NVS Stock Clocks Worst Day In Over 20 Years After Second Trial Failure In A Week — DYN, SRPT Slip In Sympathy","primary_symbol_code":"NVS","rss_syndicated":true,"sid":"cZtEeAyRJy2","source":{"id":1071,"source_name":"Stocktwits","url_domain":"stocktwits.com"},"subcategory":{"id":3,"name":"Equity","parent_id":2},"summary":"The company said on Tuesday that its experimental drug del-desiran failed in a late-stage trial. ","symbol_codes":["NVS","DYN","SRPT"],"symbols_metadata":{"DYN":{"deeplink":"symbol/DYN","logo_url":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/DYN.png","symbol":"DYN","symbol_display":"DYN","symbol_title":"Dyne Therapeutics Inc"},"NVS":{"deeplink":"symbol/NVS","logo_url":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/NVS.png","symbol":"NVS","symbol_display":"NVS","symbol_title":"Novartis AG"},"SRPT":{"deeplink":"symbol/SRPT","logo_url":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/SRPT.png","symbol":"SRPT","symbol_display":"SRPT","symbol_title":"Sarepta Therapeutics Inc"}},"tags":[{"id":2,"tag_name":"Trending"},{"id":17,"tag_name":"Equities"},{"id":19,"tag_name":"Daily"},{"id":21,"tag_name":"US"}],"type":"article","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:09:14Z","url_slug":"nvs-stock-on-track-for-worst-day-in-over-20-years-after-second-trial-failure-in-a-week-dyn-srpt-slip-in-sympathy"},{"author":{"college_name":"","college_website_url":"","country":"India","description":"Shashank is a senior staff writer at Stocktwits. He specializes in the banking, financial services and insurance (BFSI) sector and US stock market news along with reporting on leading public firms across sectors. \n\nHe is a global financial journalist and market analyst with a decade worth of experience covering the financial services industry. Previously, he was the global analyst for financial services at the Economist Intelligence Unit’s (EIU) industry analysis team. He is a specialist in forecasting and analysing bank performance indicators, stock market capitalisation, digital finance trends, insurers and reinsurerance market trends and keeping track of finance regulations. \n\nShashank’s core focus has been publishing reports and in-depth analytical articles on global equity and bond market trends with a particular focus on the insurance industry, especially with heightened climate risks rapidly altering the workings of the sector.\n","designation":"Senior Staff Writer","education":"","email":"snayar@stocktwits.com","gender":"Male","id":61,"knows_about":"","name":"Shashank Nayar","profile_avatar":"https://news.stocktwits-cdn.com/1707726834303_jpg_11f20a9aa9.webp","profile_link":"","skills":"","social_media_links":{"facebook":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shashank-nayar-27b705123/","twitter":"https://x.com/nayar_shash","website":"https://stocktwits.com/ShashankNayar"},"type":"Stocktwits"},"canonical_url":"","category":{"id":2,"name":"Markets"},"content":"\u003cul class=\"summary-bullets\"\u003e\u003cli\u003eAMD Chief Financial Officer Jean Hu stated the total addressable market for AI chips could reach $2 trillion to $3 trillion by 2030.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe company projects its data center business will more than double next year, srengthened by the launch of its MI450 GPU this quarter.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAMD expects its server CPU division to expand by more than 80% year-over-year in the second half of 2026.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdvanced Micro Devices Inc. (AMD) stock advanced about 6% on Tuesday following an optimistic long-term outlook for artificial intelligence infrastructure, projecting the overall market could hit as much as $3 trillion by the end of the decade.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSpeaking at the Citi Global TMT Conference, AMD Chief Financial Officer Jean Hu outlined an accelerated expansion strategy. While the semiconductor manufacturer had previously estimated in July that its addressable market would reach around $2 trillion by 2030, Hu signaled that surging adoption across the tech sector could push that figure significantly higher to between $2 trillion and $3 trillion.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAMD shares climbed 6% to 7%, extending a rally that has more than doubled the stock over the year.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“This AI super investment cycle is at the very beginning, and over time, we’re going to continue to see strong demand for AMD’s product,” the chief financial officer said.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“It’s a very exciting time for AMD,” Hu added.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShifting AI Landscape Drives Demand\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt the heart of AMD’s updated projections is a fundamental shift in how artificial intelligence workloads are processed. Computing requirements are rapidly transitioning from initial model training to live inference—the execution of deployed AI models. Hu noted that over the past year, inference has become the primary operational engine for AI deployment, shifting from simple conversational tools to autonomous, agent-based enterprise applications.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo capitalize on this structural transition, AMD is accelerating its hardware deployment schedule. The company plans to release its next-generation MI450 AI accelerator GPU this quarter, with production ramp-ups extending through the fourth quarter and into 2027. Furthermore, AMD has secured preliminary commitments for its server systems from major technology clients, including Meta Platforms, with client projections outpacing initial purchase agreements.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStrong Momentum Across Core Segments\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeyond graphics processors, AMD’s traditional chip architectures are seeing accelerated momentum. The company has boosted output in formerly supply-constrained central processing unit (CPU) markets, projecting its server CPU line to grow by more than 80% year-over-year in the second half of this year and over 70% next year. Overall, AMD expects its broader data center segment to more than double in size over the coming year.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhile initial gross margins on high-end data center GPUs remain slightly below AMD’s overall corporate average, strong double-digit growth in high-margin server and embedded solutions has maintained strong enterprise profitability. Looking further ahead, management confirmed ongoing customer technical engagements for future hardware architectures, including the upcoming MI500 and MI600 series.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"st-heading-2\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAMD Stock: Retail View\u0026nbsp;\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eRetail sentiment on Stocktwits was ‘neutral’ with ‘normal’ message volumes.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://stocktwits.com/symbol/AMD\"\u003eAMD stock\u003c/a\u003e has surged 139% year-to-date.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRead More: \u003ca href=\"https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/hsbc-hikes-s-and-p-500-s-2026-price-target-sees-about-5-more-upside-on-strong-earnings/cZtEP7xRJUx\"\u003eHSBC Hikes S\u0026amp;P 500’s 2026 Price Target, Sees About 5% More Upside On Strong Earnings\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eFor updates and corrections, email newsroom[at]stocktwits[dot]com\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","created_at":"2026-09-08T19:57:48Z","featured_image":"https://news.stocktwits-cdn.com/large_Getty_Images_2285958555_jpg_3b020b5c3e.webp","featured_image_attributes":{"alt_text":"AMD logo at its office building in Zhongguancun, Beijing, China. (Photo credit should read Stringer/Future Publishing via Getty Images)","caption":"AMD logo at its office building in Zhongguancun, Beijing, China. (Photo credit should read Stringer/Future Publishing via Getty Images)","url":"https://news.stocktwits-cdn.com/large_Getty_Images_2285958555_jpg_3b020b5c3e.webp"},"headline":"AMD Stock Spikes 6% After CFO Claims Total Addressable Market To Hit $3 Trillion In 2030 ","hero_article":true,"image_url":"https://st-everywhere-cms-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/large_Getty_Images_2285958555_jpg_3b020b5c3e.webp","is_amp":true,"is_indexed":true,"meta_description":"Advanced Micro Devices stock jumped over 6% following executive statements detailing a massive expansion in artificial intelligence infrastructure demand and an aggressive multi-year hardware rollout strategy.","meta_keywords":"amd, amd stock, advanced micro devices","meta_title":"AMD Stock Spikes 6% After CFO Claims Total Addressable Market To Hit $3 Trillion In 2030","primary_symbol_code":"AMD","rss_syndicated":true,"sid":"cZtEIhVRJyc","source":{"id":1071,"source_name":"Stocktwits","url_domain":"stocktwits.com"},"subcategory":{"id":3,"name":"Equity","parent_id":2},"summary":"Advanced Micro Devices stock jumped over 6% following executive statements detailing a massive expansion in artificial intelligence infrastructure demand and an aggressive multi-year hardware rollout strategy. ","symbol_codes":["AMD"],"symbols_metadata":{"AMD":{"deeplink":"symbol/AMD","logo_url":"https://logos.stocktwits-cdn.com/AMD.png","symbol":"AMD","symbol_display":"AMD","symbol_title":"Advanced Micro Devices Inc"}},"tags":[{"id":2,"tag_name":"Trending"},{"id":17,"tag_name":"Equities"},{"id":21,"tag_name":"US"}],"type":"article","updated_at":"2026-09-08T19:57:48Z","url_slug":"amd-stock-spikes-6-after-cfo-claims-total-addressable-market-to-hit-3-trillion-in-2030"},{"author":{"college_name":"University of Calcutta","college_website_url":"","country":"India","description":"Aveek Bhowmik is a journalist, writer and editor with around 20 years of experience across Indian and international media organizations. He is currently a Senior Staff Writer at Stocktwits.\n\nIn the past, he has worked as a Desk Editor at Benzinga, where he also wrote on US financial markets, consumer technology, political developments, stocks and corporate news. \n\nOver the course of his career, he has worked with leading Indian media organizations including The Times of India, The Telegraph, Hindustan Times and The Economic Times, where he led teams and managed editions.","designation":"Senior Staff Writer","education":"BCom","email":"abhowmik@stocktwits.com","gender":"Male","id":64,"knows_about":"Consumer Tech, Materials, Auto","name":"Aveek Bhowmik","profile_avatar":"https://news.stocktwits-cdn.com/Whats_App_Image_2026_05_11_at_09_45_43_1_jpeg_a08c0cf251.webp","profile_link":"","skills":"Reporting, Writing, Editing, Interviewing, Content Writing, Content Strategy, Research","social_media_links":{"facebook":"linkedin.com/in/aveek-bhowmik-06114ab1","twitter":"https://x.com/Aveekishere","website":"https://stocktwits.com/Aveek_Bhowmik"},"type":"Stocktwits"},"canonical_url":"","category":{"id":2,"name":"Markets"},"content":"\u003cul class=\"summary-bullets\"\u003e\u003cli\u003eLa Bola Negra will reportedly get Netflix’s longest theatrical rollout yet, with a 46-day run before its streaming release.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eNarnia is set for a nearly 50-day wide run, including IMAX, in 2027, while Charlie and the Chocolate Factory will play wide for 47 days at Christmas.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eNetflix has historically favored limited theatrical releases and did not disclose box office figures, drawing resistance from cinema operators over its theatrical strategy.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eNetflix (NFLX) will report box office grosses for six upcoming films as the streaming giant expands theatrical runs for several releases